TEST 8770 -- IPv6 Neighbors - in silicon
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-22, tb470

VERDICT: UNMEASURED -- BENCH LIMIT, not a product or scope issue.

The case's method names the tool and the scale directly: "Use IxExplorer to
emulate Maximum IPv6 Neighbors. Consult with limits database for maximum number
of IPv6 neighbors for DUT (this is approximately 5000)."

Two hard requirements this bench cannot meet:
 1. ~5000 emulated IPv6 neighbours. There is one host NIC on the ingress port.
 2. Neighbours that actually RESPOND to neighbour discovery -- the DUT populates
    its neighbour table from real exchanges, exactly as it declines to learn
    ARP from unsolicited frames (see switching T6057, where 6000 gratuitous ARPs
    produced zero entries). Crafted one-way frames will not fill the table.

WHAT IS PROVEN ELSEWHERE: IPv6 neighbour discovery works correctly -- T8734
shows the DUT answering a Neighbor Solicitation with a properly-flagged
Neighbor Advertisement (S=1, O=1). Scale is the gap, not function.

TO UNBLOCK: an ixia or equivalent emulating thousands of responding neighbours.
